
Things we need to include for sure:
* Add a TodoItem record, sqlite backed, endpoints (/list, /details, /update)
* Add a UI
    * Single-page, one giant list of items, a little form for adding new ones
      at the bottom, each item can be closed or open, when open you can edit
      it & save it.
* Tests
    * https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/aspnet/core/fundamentals/minimal-apis/test-min-api?view=aspnetcore-10.0
    * https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/aspnet/core/mvc/controllers/testing?view=aspnetcore-10.0
    * UI needs unit tests w/ DOM stuff, e.g. Jest for the general test framework,
      Enzyme for testing React components (e.g. shallow component rendering)
    * e2e tests also possible, e.g. via Postman, Bruno, Hurl...
* Accessibility
    * E.g. internationalization... I searched "react i18n" and found: https://react.i18next.com/
* Support for different devices

Optional stuff:
* Pagination
* Local cache of TODO items, so we don't need so many API calls
* Docker compose for backend + frontend (and later, HL7 listener)
* Add images to each TodoItem, UI component for drawing outlines on them
* Add an HL7 listener
    https://saravanansubramanian.com/blog/hl72xdotnetprogramming/
    https://github.com/nHapiNET/nHapi
    https://github.com/dib0/NHapiTools
    https://github.com/dib0/HL7Fuse
